{% extends "commons/base.njk" %}

{#
  A driver's tab: on the left the projects that are theirs to act on, on the right the links
  they hand out.

  Two columns because the two answer different questions — «what is there for me to do» and
  «how do I bring somebody in» — and stacking them made the second read as a step of the
  first. On a narrow screen the column falls under the lists: the projects are the reason
  the page is opened.

  Two lists and not three. A project of theirs in `DEVELOPMENT`, `DEMO` or `PAID` is read
  and not shown: the lists that will hold it belong to the gates that do not exist yet, and
  a third list now would be a page built for work nothing can do.
#}

{% block header_extra %}{% include "partials/nav.njk" %}{% endblock %}

{% block main %}
    <div class="container projects">
      <h1>{{ heading }}</h1>

      {#-
        What was just decided at the gate. The project it was about has left both lists —
        an approved one is the client's to answer now, a refused one is closed — so
        without this the driver would press confirm and watch a row disappear with nothing
        said about it.
      -#}
      {%- if decided %}
      <p class="decided-notice" role="status">{{ decided }}</p>
      {%- endif %}

      <div class="two-columns">
        <div class="column-main">
          {% set group_title = t("projects_hub.driver.waiting.title") %}
          {% set group_empty = t("projects_hub.driver.waiting.empty") %}
          {% set group_projects = waiting %}
          {% include "partials/project_group.njk" %}

          {% set group_title = t("projects_hub.driver.failed.title") %}
          {% set group_empty = t("projects_hub.driver.failed.empty") %}
          {% set group_projects = failed %}
          {% set group_muted = true %}
          {% include "partials/project_group.njk" %}
        </div>

        <aside class="column-side" aria-label="{{ t('projects_hub.driver.links.title') }}">
          {% include "partials/links.njk" %}
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
